# pnpm & Workflow

## Package manager

Use **pnpm** only. Do not introduce npm/yarn commands.

Prefer: `pnpm install`, `pnpm add`, `pnpm remove`, `pnpm dev`, `pnpm build`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`.

Do not upgrade dependencies without justification. Respect `pnpm-workspace.yaml` and Turbo.

## Feature workflow

1. Inspect → 2. Plan → 3. Implement → 4. Validate → 5. Test → 6. Lint → 7. Typecheck → 8. Review → 9. Fix → 10. Summarize

## Before finishing

Run relevant: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm build` (or project-equivalent scripts). Fix errors you introduced. Do not claim success if validation fails.

## Git safety

Do not `reset --hard`, force-push, delete branches/migrations, or overwrite unrelated changes without explicit approval. Keep diffs focused.

## Response summary (after a task)

What Changed · Files Created/Modified · Database · API · Frontend · Security/RBAC · Tests · Validation · Remaining Issues — factual only.
